# C# Code Style

## Naming

| Kind | Style | Example |
|------|-------|---------|
| Private / protected fields (incl. `[SerializeField]`) | `_camelCase` | `_hudController`, `_spacing` |
| Constants, `static readonly`, public members, types, methods | `PascalCase` | `MaxLanes`, `ByScore`, `CardCount`, `Fire()` |
| Locals, parameters | `camelCase` | `lane`, `targetId` |
| Event handlers | `On<Event>` | `OnRoundEnded`, `OnFireClicked` |
| Task/Awaitable-returning methods | `Async` suffix | `LoadProfileAsync()` |
| May-fail lookups | `Try*` with `out` | `TryGetUnit(id, out var unit)` |
| Bool members | question form | `IsStunned`, `HasInstance`, `CanFire` |

No `s_`/`m_` prefixes, no Hungarian, no type names in identifiers (`_unitList`). Interfaces keep the `I` prefix (and need a justification — see the no-premature-abstraction rule).

## No one-liner if statements

Always use braces for `if`, `else if`, and `else` bodies — even single statements.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
if (x) DoThing();
if (x) return;

// ✅ GOOD
if (x)
{
    DoThing();
}
```

Ternary (`?:`) is fine.

## Explicit `private` modifier

Never rely on the implicit default access level. Write `private` on every private field, method, property, and nested type.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
int _count;
void Recalculate() { }

// ✅ GOOD
private int _count;
private void Recalculate() { }
```

## Member order — fields first

Within a type, declare **fields before** properties, constructors, and methods. Group all fields at the top (constants, statics, serialized, instance). Nested types go at the bottom.

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
public class HandLayout : MonoBehaviour
{
    [SerializeField] private float _spacing;
    private readonly List<CardView> _cards = new();

    public int CardCount => _cards.Count;

    private void Awake() { }
}
```

## No premature util classes

Do not create a static helper/util class for logic used in **one place**. Keep it inline or as a private method on the type that needs it. Extract to a shared helper only when the same logic is duplicated in **at least two** call sites.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — new CardNaming.cs for a single call site
go.name = $"Card_{CardNaming.DisplayName(card)}";

// ✅ GOOD — local until a second site needs it
go.name = $"Card_{FormatCardName(card)}";
```

## No one-line wrapper methods

Do not extract a method whose entire body is a single call to another method with the same arguments. Call the target directly.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Names follow the table: `_camelCase` fields, `PascalCase` statics/consts/members, `On*` handlers, `*Async`, `Try*`
- [ ] No `if (…) statement;` without braces in new or edited code
- [ ] `private` written explicitly on all private members
- [ ] Fields declared before properties and methods within each type
- [ ] No new util class or wrapper method for single-call-site logic
